Database migrations (Alembic). Run every command from the project root.

    alembic upgrade head                                        apply all migrations
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "orders" --rev-id 0002   new migration from model changes
    alembic upgrade head --sql                                  print the SQL instead of running it
    alembic check                                               fail if models and migrations differ
    alembic downgrade -1                                        undo the latest migration

Rules of the road:

- Change the SQLAlchemy models first, then autogenerate, then read the generated file.
  Autogenerate misses some things (renames look like drop + add, extensions, data moves).
- Number revisions in order with --rev-id (0002, 0003, ...).
- A model in a new domain package must be imported in store/metadata.py, or Alembic
  will not see its tables.
- tests/test_migrations.py fails when models and migrations disagree.
